cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its manuscript reproducibility package, please cite the archived software release and associated manuscript."
title: "EnerMat Explorer: reproducibility package for uncertainty-aware multi-objective screening of Sn-Ge halide perovskites"
version: 3.0.0
date-released: 2026-09-20
url: https://github.com/omogbadebowale/EnerMat-Explorer
repository-code: https://github.com/omogbadebowale/EnerMat-Explorer.git
license: MIT
type: software
keywords:
  - perovskites
  - photovoltaics
  - tin-germanium
  - materials screening
  - uncertainty analysis
  - multi-objective decision analysis
  - Pareto analysis
  - model-form uncertainty
  - reproducibility
authors:
  - family-names: Yusuf
    given-names: Gbadebo Taofeek
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0000-0002-9532-8134
abstract: >
  EnerMat Explorer v3.0.0 contains the final manuscript reproducibility package for
  uncertainty-aware multi-objective screening of 231 lead-free Sn-Ge mixed-halide
  perovskite compositions. The release includes literature-informed band-gap
  calibration, interpolation-based phase-stability and oxidation screening proxies,
  explicit composite-score mathematics, 10,000-draw scoring-model sensitivity
  analyses, a 5,000-draw descriptor-calibration stress test, a weight-free Pareto
  diagnostic, Latin-hypercube convergence testing, an independent synthesis-resolved
  bromide optical challenge, and a 10,000-draw nonlinear model-form stress test with
  anchor-preserving curvature in the stability/oxidation proxy surfaces. The release
  is a transparent materials-prioritisation and robustness framework; no new
  composition-specific DFT calculations were performed for the inherited
  stability/oxidation corner inputs.
